      "id": 1,
      "text": "The McGehee family arrived from Alabama in 1857, laying the groundwork for the town that would bear their name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McGehee%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Abner McGehee bought 240 acres in 1876 and built a commissary that became the town’s first commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McGehee%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad reached McGehee in 1878, sparking a population boom as people moved in along the new line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McGehee%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office opened in the commissary in 1879, with Abner McGehee as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McGehee%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "McGehee was officially incorporated on March 5, 1906, and its first town council met on July 21 that year.",
